Frame interpolation in the dungeon.

The interpolator matched only 1 of ~108 dungeon polygons, so "interpolated"
frames repeated the last game frame (Baroque draws a new 3D frame every third
field, 20 fps). Two causes:

1. Identity required the same colr (colour bank / lookup-table address).
   Baroque double-buffers its lighting tables, so colr changes every frame.
   Identity and the texture-reuse hash now ignore colour tables; the replay
   always draws with the current frame's tables.
2. geometry_weld held any edge shared by more than two faces, freezing the
   whole connected room. Baroque's ceiling trim meets the wall panels above
   and below it. Distinct faces on one edge are now allowed when all their
   histories agree; stacked duplicate faces are still held, as before.

tests/geometry_interp.c gains a three-face case.

